<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="009" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Repair the office-addins jest harness (jest-dom registration) and re-measure the test-file debt</title>
    <phase>0 De-risk and baseline</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies test configuration and `tests/`-adjacent files. The CLAUDE.md §8 TEST-MODIFYING override applies: code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5 run UNCONDITIONALLY regardless of rigor tier.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>A configuration repair with a known cause and a measurable outcome. Escalate only if the missing registration turns out not to be the cause.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P0-typecheck</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches jest setup/config and test files only. Tasks 006/007/008 are re-scoped to PRODUCTION sources and are explicitly forbidden from touching test files, so the file sets are disjoint.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>office-addins, testing, test-harness, tooling</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Repair the `src/client/office-addins` jest harness so the suite runs, then RE-MEASURE the test-file typecheck debt and report what remains. Do not fix test-file type errors in this task — measuring honestly is the deliverable.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer. Expertise in jest + ts-jest + React Testing Library configuration. Follow ADR-038; a test that asserts nothing is worse than no test.</role>

  <goal>`npm test` in `src/client/office-addins` runs with the jest-dom matchers registered, the suite's pass/fail state is honestly reported, and `notes/009-jest-harness-repair.md` records the before/after suite counts plus a re-measured test-file typecheck count with a recommendation on whether the residual warrants its own task.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Created 2026-09-09 by operator decision B1. FR-18 was narrowed to PRODUCTION types (88 errors, owned by tasks 006/007/008). That decision deliberately left the test-side debt — 296 of 384 typecheck errors — without an owner. Leaving it unowned would be burial-by-omission, which this project's deferral policy forbids. This task owns it.

      Task 001's baseline (`notes/typecheck-baseline.md`) recorded: `npm test` fails at baseline with **13 of 21 suites** and **57 of 226 tests** failing, attributed to a **missing `jest-dom` registration**. Its Recommendation 5 states the harness gap should be fixed SEPARATELY from FR-18 and predicts the single setup change "likely clears a large share of both the 57 test failures and some TS2339 count".

      That prediction is a HYPOTHESIS, not a finding. This task's job is to test it and report the real number — not to assume it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-baseline.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/jest.config.js</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/package.json</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="complete">Supplied the baseline suite and typecheck counts this task measures against.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Build commands: `npm run build` IS the production build — there is no `build:prod` in this package. Installs use `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`; never `npm ci` (root CLAUDE.md §12).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — repair the HARNESS. Do NOT fix test-file type errors, and do NOT rewrite test bodies to make them pass. If a test fails on a real product defect after the harness is fixed, that is a FINDING to report, not something to edit away.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST NOT touch any file under `shared/taskpane/**`, `shared/adapters/**`, `shared/services/**`, `word/**` or `outlook/**` that is NOT a test file — tasks 006/007/008 own those production sources and run concurrently with this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="adr">ADR-038 — never delete or skip a failing test to make a suite green. A `Skip` requires a recorded reason. Deleting coverage to reach a number is the exact anti-pattern the testing strategy bans.</constraint>
    <constraint source="adr">CLAUDE.md §8 TEST-MODIFYING override — Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check run UNCONDITIONALLY for this task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Report the suite result HONESTLY. If the jest-dom registration is not the whole cause, say so and quantify what remains. A partial repair truthfully reported is a success; an overstated one is not.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The missing jest-dom registration turns out NOT to be the cause of the 13 failing suites. Stop, report the real cause with evidence, and do not begin an open-ended test-repair campaign under this task's name.</trigger>
    <trigger>Fixing the harness requires a dependency bump that changes React or @testing-library major versions. That is a package-graph decision (the project is on React 19 with @testing-library/react@14 peer-requiring 18) — escalate rather than resolving it unilaterally.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm test` in `src/client/office-addins` runs to completion with jest-dom matchers registered; the before/after suite and test counts are recorded verbatim.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The test-file typecheck count is RE-MEASURED after the repair (baseline: 296 of 384 on 2026-09-09) and the new number is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/009-jest-harness-repair.md` states whether task 001's hypothesis held, and recommends either (a) the residual test debt needs its own task, or (b) it is small enough to fold into an existing one — with the count that justifies the call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No production source file was modified — verified by `git status` showing changes only to test files and jest/package configuration.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No test was deleted or newly skipped to reach a green number (ADR-038).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">Any test failing on a genuine product defect after the repair is reported as a finding, not edited away.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">src/client/office-addins/jest.config.js</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/009-jest-harness-repair.md</output>
  </outputs>
</task>
